      "side": 1,
      "message": "This logic looks correct to me, except that we need to handle aligning instances too. Unlike the follow-up ARM execution bug, we do want to adjusting this value to minimize binding buffers for both appended vertex data or instance data.\n\nWe should be able to infer which stride to use for alignment based on `fTemplateCount \u003d\u003d 0` for the prior state (\u003d\u003d 0 means we were doing vertex only draws), and for the new pipeline state if `instanceStride \u003d\u003d 0` we would be doing vertex data. It doesn\u0027t make much sense (and we can add asserts) that we don\u0027t ever create a DrawWriter::Instances() with an instance stride of 0.",
